{{also|Wool}}
==English==
[[File:BladeShearing.jpg|thumb|A sheep being shorn for its wool.]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂welh₁-|id=wool}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wolle}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wull}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wullu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wullō}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂wĺ̥h₁neh₂}}. 

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|Wulle}}, {{cog|nds-de|Wull}}, {{cog|nl|wol}}, {{cog|de|Wolle}}, {{cog|no|ull}}; also {{cog|cy|gwlân}}, {{cog|la|lāna}}, {{cog|lt|vìlna}}, {{cog|ru|во́лос}}, {{cog|sk|vlna}}, {{cog|bg|влас}}, {{cog|sq|lesh||wool, hair, fleece}}. {{doublet|en|lana}}. {{rel-bottom}}

The vowel development ''u'' → ''o'' → ''oo'' is purely graphical. Modern English generally avoids the string ‹wu› in favour of ‹wo›, and the resulting ''woll'' was then altered to ''wool'' (as supposedly better representing the pronunciation). 

